<title>UK: UK's FTSE 100 index set for ex-dividend blow.</title>
<headline>UK's FTSE 100 index set for ex-dividend blow.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following FTSE 100 stocks will go ex-dividend on March 17 and analysts estimate the effect will be to take 22.09 points off the index that day.</p>
<p>					    DIVIDEND	INDEX</p>
<p>					    (PENCE)	 EFFECT</p>
<p>COMPANY				  Net   Gross    Gross * BAT Industries		     (a)   20.000   3.620</p>
<p>* BTR				    (b)    7.000   1.638</p>
<p>* Cadbury Schweppes		11.80   14.750   0.856 </p>
<p>* GKN				  16.90   21.125   0.021 </p>
<p>* Glaxo Wellcome		     (c)   22.563   4.670</p>
<p>* HSBC Holdings		    26.00   32.500   1.658</p>
<p>* HSBC Holdings ($HK)	    26.00   32.500   3.380</p>
<p>* Ladbroke Group		    3.80    4.750   0.323</p>
<p>* RTZ Corporation		    (d)   23.110   1.433</p>
<p>* Reuters Holdings		  9.00   11.250   1.103</p>
<p>* Royal &amp; Sun Alliance	   12.50   15.625   1.422</p>
<p>* Zeneca Group		     22.50   28.125   1.547</p>
<p>(a) For BAT Industries the total dividend amount is 19.5p and includes 17.5p Foreign Income Dividend (FID).</p>
<p>(b) For BTR the dividend is an FID of 7p only.</p>
<p>(c) For Glaxo Wellcome the total dividend amount is 19p and includes an FID of 475p.</p>
<p>(d) For RTZ Corporation the total dividend amount is 13.11p and includes an FID of 21.11p.</p>
</text>
